title: Young Plan
new-page: true
subtitle: A new agreement on reparations
tags: event
view-if: year = 1929 and month >= 7 and in_right_coalition = 0 and young_plan_seen = 0 and dnvp_leader = "Hugenberg" 
on-arrival: young_plan_seen = 1
max-visits: 1

= Young Plan

The Young Plan is an agreement with the Western powers to reduce Germany's reparation payments and give us more fiscal autonomy. Simultaneously, France will agree to withdraw its military occupation from the Rhineland.

While this seems to be a positive development for the country, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Nationalist Right</span> led by Hugenburg has started a campaign opposing the Young Plan. By presenting the Young Plan as a plot to enslave Germany for generations to come, Hugenburg's "<i>Katastrophenpolitik</i>" aims to polarise the electorate. Nevertheless, the passaage of the Young Plan is of utmost priority in relation to Germany's financial situation. 

- @government: With our federal coalition partners, utilise the resources of the federal government to campaign for the Young Plan.
- @prussia: With our federal coalition partners and <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> Coalition parties in Prussia, utilise the resources of the federal government and Prussia to campaign for the Young Plan.
- @bourgeois: Monopolise the campaign in favor of the Young Plan with the other bourgeois parties, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>.
- @no_plan: Do not campaign on the Young Plan, one way or another.

@government
on-arrival: coalition_dissent -= 1; dnvp_relation -= 3; workers_spd += 2; dvp_left += 0.5; nationalism += 5; dvp_young_plan_modifier -= 0.005; dvp_young_plan_modifier -= 0.005 if dvp_in_government = 1; young_plan_modifier -= 0.01

Due to this crusade against the Young Plan causing much civil unrest, inaction while the Hugenberg Media Empire attempts to destroy the late Stressemann’s legacy would be unwise. With the resources of the state at our disposal and some support from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, the government has united in a vigorous defense of the Young Plan, pouring 495 000 marks into running a substantial media campaign to counter the propaganda of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> and their allies. 

Together with the moderate bourgeois parties, we issue a public statement denouncing the so-called Freedom Law as a “laughable miscarriage” that seeks only to divide rather than unite the German people, with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD’s**</span> going all out in their castigation of Hugenberg’s  <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. In an appeal in support of the Young Plan organised by the government, we have managed to garner the support  of all the cabinet officers and other well-known public figures, including indus trialist Robert Bosch, Albert Einstein and Max Planck from the German scientific community, historians Hermann Oncken and Friedrich Meinecke, dramatist Gerhard Hauptmann, and Nobel laureate Thomas Mann. Despite that, the signatures of prominent industrialists like Carl Duisburg and Carl Friedrich von Siemens remain notably absent. Although they have disagreements with the tone and substance of Hugenberg’s campaign, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD’s**</span> monopolisation of this campaign has left them silent. 

Having done all that we can, the responsibility now falls on the people to vote, vote, vote against this kind of reckless demagoguery.

@prussia
choose-if: spd_in_prussia == 1 and z_in_prussia == 1 and weimar_coalition_prussia = 1
subtitle: The Prussian Cabinet can make the campaign more effective. 
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dvp_in_prussia == 1 and dnvp_in_prussia == 0 : While the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> supports the Young Plan, they fear being closely associated with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>. ?][? if dvp_in_prussia == 1 and dnvp_in_prussia == 1 : The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Bürgerbloc**</span>	will collapse if we attempt to do this. ?]
on-arrival: spd_relation += 3; workers_spd += 3; dnvp_relation -= 5; left_strength += 3; right_dissent += 4; dvp_left += 1; nationalism += 3; dvp_young_plan_modifier -= 0.008; young_plan_modifier -= 0.015

Due to this crusade against the Young Plan causing much civil unrest, inaction while the Hugenberg Media Empire attempts to destroy the late Stressemann’s legacy would be unwise. With the resources of the state at our disposal and some support from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, the government has poured 495 000 marks into running a substantial media campaign to counter the propaganda of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> and their allies. 

Complementing the government-funded campaign is the incumbent <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> Coalition in Prussia, which pressures regional newspapers into printing editorials calling for a "No" vote on Hugenberg's Young Plan Referendum, with Braun addressing the Prussian people on radio urging the voters not to support the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Stahlhelm's**</span> action. Under orders from Prussian Interior Minister Albert Grzesinski, all political appointees in the Prussian civil service have also been barred from offering support and have been required to  sign petitions opposing this radical initiative. While the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP’s**</span> Prussian Landtag Delegation criticize our politicisation of the Prussian civil service, their attempts to reverse these orders have been soundly defeated by the votes of the <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> Coalition Partners and that of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>.

Together with the moderate bourgeois parties, we issued a public statement denouncing the so-called Freedom Law as a “laughable miscarriage” that seeks only to divide rather than unite the German people, with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD’s**</span> going all out in their castigation of Hugenberg’s  <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. In an appeal in support of the Young Plan organised by the government, we have managed to garner the support  of all the cabinet officers and other well-known public figures, including indus trialist Robert Bosch, Albert Einstein and Max Planck from the German scientific community, historians Hermann Oncken and Friedrich Meinecke, dramatist Gerhard Hauptmann, and Nobel laureate Thomas Mann. Despite that, the signatures of prominent industrialists like Carl Duisburg and Carl Friedrich von Siemens remain notably absent. Although they have disagreements with the tone and substance of Hugenberg’s campaign, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD’s**</span> of this campaign has left them silent. 

Having done all that we can, the responsibility now falls on the people to vote, vote, vote against this kind of reckless demagoguery.

@bourgeois
subtitle: This would sideline the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>, displeasing the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Christian Left</span>. 
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 4; ddp_relation += 2; dvp_relation += 2; dnvp_relation -= 3; center_dissent -= 4; center_strength += 4; left_dissent += 3; left_strength -= 3; ddp_right += 2; dvp_left += 2; rdi_balance -= 4; old_middle_dvp += 1; new_middle_ddp += 1; catholics_z += 1/5; nationalism += 5; dvp_young_plan_modifier -= 0.026; young_plan_modifier -= 0.01

Due to this crusade against the Young Plan causing much civil unrest, inaction while the Hugenberg Media Empire attempts to destroy the late Stressemann’s legacy would be unwise. With the resources of the state at our disposal and some support from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, the government has poured 495 000 marks into running a substantial media campaign to counter the propaganda of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> and their allies. 

Together with the moderate bourgeois parties, we have issued a public statement denouncing the so-called Freedom Law as a “laughable miscarriage” that sought only to divide rather than unite the German people. Furthermore, we have organised an appeal in support of the Young Plan which has garnered the signatures of all the cabinet officers and other well-known public figures, including indus trialist Robert Bosch, Albert Einstein and Max Planck from the German scientific community, historians Hermann Oncken and Friedrich Meinecke, dramatist Gerhard Hauptmann, and Nobel laureate Thomas Mann. Due to the relatively bourgeois character of this campaign, in which the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> has not played a major role in, we have even managed to garner the signatures of prominent industrialists like Carl Duisberg and Carl Friedrich von Siemens, ensuring solid backing from the political center. 

Having done all that we can, the responsibility now falls on the people to vote, vote, vote against this kind of reckless demagoguery.

@no_plan
on-arrival: nationalism += 7; workers_z -= 1; new_middle_z -= 1; pacifism -= 1; workers_nsdap += 2; rural_nsdap += 2; workers_spd += 3; new_middle_ddp += 1; catholics_z -= 3; dnvp_relation += 3; dvp_relation -= 3; spd_relation -= 5; ddp_relations -= 5; left_dissent += 8; labor_dissent += 3; center_dissent += 5
subtitle: The majority of our party is strongly against this course of action

Our left and labor factions are united in an uproar against this and many have broken with the party to denounce this initiative. Meanwhile, our center and right are uneasy over our tacit approval of Hugenberg's actions As a 'natural governing party', our inaction on such an issue is met with confusion from outside observers
